  "unknowns": [
    {
      "id": "U-01",
      "question": "Is `validate` subject to the state machine at all? The text names it as an operation on a request (line 68) but not as a transition, and the general rule (lines 24–25) literally makes every unlisted (from, action) pair illegal with 409. In which states is validate allowed, does it change state, and what does it return in the others?",
      "affects": [
        "ST-08",
        "ST-16",
        "ST-24",
        "ST-32",
        "ST-40",
        "ST-48",
        "ST-56"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-02",
      "question": "SUBMITTED is transient and \"never observed at rest\" (lines 31, 51), yet SUBMITTED → cancel is listed as legal \"in the narrow window before gates resolve it\" (line 38). Can a caller ever reach that window (gates run synchronously in the submit call)? If not, how are the SUBMITTED-row cells (cancel legal; submit/approve/reject/complete illegal) meant to be tested, or should they be excluded?",
      "affects": [
        "ST-09",
        "ST-12",
        "ST-13",
        "ST-14",
        "ST-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-03",
      "question": "Gate pass/fail are automatic events, not caller actions (line 32). The general rule makes them illegal outside SUBMITTED, but nothing can trigger them there. How should these cells be verified (e.g. gates never re-run on other states), and is a 409 meaningful for them?",
      "affects": [
        "ST-02",
        "ST-03",
        "ST-18",
        "ST-19",
        "ST-26",
        "ST-27",
        "ST-34",
        "ST-35",
        "ST-42",
        "ST-43",
        "ST-50",
        "ST-51"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-04",
      "question": "What precision does the 2-hour cancellation deadline use (hours, minutes, seconds), and which clock/time zone is compared with window_start? Needed to place the values just inside and just outside 2 hours more tightly than 1 hour.",
      "affects": [
        "BV-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-05",
      "question": "How is cancelling an APPROVED request handled when window_start has already passed (or the window has ended but no completion was recorded)? The text only defines \"2 hours or more before\" and \"closer than 2 hours\".",
      "affects": [
        "EP-09",
        "EP-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-06",
      "question": "What does the system return when approve or reject is called without X-Reviewer-Id (e.g. by an operator session), and does it matter if both an operator session and X-Reviewer-Id are sent? The text says only \"Reviewer-only\".",
      "affects": [
        "EP-04",
        "EP-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-07",
      "question": "What does the system return when reject is called without a note, and how are an empty or whitespace-only note, or an over-long note, handled? The text says only \"`note` required\".",
      "affects": [
        "EP-08"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-08",
      "question": "Cancel is \"Operator-initiated\" (lines 37–40). Is that a restriction (a reviewer or a different operator may not cancel)? If so, what is returned? Does cancel need any fields (e.g. a reason)?",
      "affects": [
        "ST-07",
        "ST-15",
        "ST-23",
        "ST-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-09",
      "question": "What does the submit call return (status code and body) when a gate fails and the request goes to REJECTED, and when all gates pass and it goes to UNDER_REVIEW? The text names only the fields `failing_gate`/`rejection_reason`.",
      "affects": [
        "EP-01",
        "EP-02",
        "ST-10",
        "ST-11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-10",
      "question": "For the aircraft overlap check: which gate reports the failure (AIRCRAFT or TIME_WINDOW, line 66), what counts as an overlap (touching windows?), and is a request in SUBMITTED (not listed in either group) counted?",
      "affects": [
        "EP-13",
        "EP-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "U-11",
      "question": "Who may call the maintenance completion endpoint, is there any time condition on complete (e.g. only after window_end), and what does it return when called on a non-APPROVED request beyond the general 409?",
      "affects": [
        "EP-11",
        "ST-30"
      ]
    }
  ]
